HYPOTHESIS APlayerIdentifierIsASteamAccountReusedAcrossGames
	DESC "a player identifier is a Steam account identifier, which the game reuses from one game to"
		+ "the next and which is unique neither across two saves nor, formally, within one"
	UNTIL "a save whose player identifier names no Steam account, or two saves of the same account"
		+ "carrying different identifiers"
	SOURCE "Extracted from the ruling on player identity, decision of 2026-09-07, pull request 39,"
		+ "recorded on 2026-09-18"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST39

HYPOTHESIS AWorldObjectMayCarryALinkedObjectList
	DESC "a world object may carry woIds, the list of the world objects it holds"
	UNTIL "a source shows that the contents of a world object are only ever reached through its"
		+ "linked inventory"
	RATIONALE "The property appears on none of the 190338 world object entries surveyed: either it"
		+ "exists and the sample does not meet it, or it does not exist and the contents go through"
		+ "the linked inventory. It stays declared as a precaution: under a schema closed to"
		+ "additional properties, omitting it would reject a save that the reference rewrite claims"
		+ "to handle. If refuted, the type, the reference remapping and the matching line of the"
		+ "identifier rule go together, not the schema alone"
	SOURCE "Found on 2026-09-10, left open in the review of pull request 48, recorded on 2026-09-18"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST48

HYPOTHESIS AnAnimalHungerLevelLiesBetweenMinus100And100
	DESC "the hunger level of an animal lies between -100 and 100"
	UNTIL "a legitimate save is rejected by the hunger bounds"
	OBSERVED_IN "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/section3-world-objects.schema.json::ranging"
		+ "from -100 to 94.22"
	RATIONALE "The field was observed on the entries of a single group identifier only, 345"
		+ "occurrences over 190338, ranging from -100 to 94.22. The symmetric scale rests on an"
		+ "animal yielding a DNA sequence when its level is positive, which is consistent with a"
		+ "ceiling without proving it. It is exactly the risk the schema rule names, a bound set on"
		+ "the sample alone rejecting a legitimate save; the user accepted that risk"
		REF @DECISION.ASchemaRuleHoldsByMeaningBeforeMeasurement
	SOURCE "Found on 2026-09-10 in pull request 48, recorded on 2026-09-18"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST48

HYPOTHESIS ProceduralWrecksAreSpawnedByThePortalGenerator
	DESC "the ProceduralWreck objects and ProceduralInstanceGenerator are spawned by"
		+ "PortalGenerator1, the portal generator"
	UNTIL "a save or a game source shows procedural wrecks spawned without PortalGenerator1"
	RATIONALE "ProceduralInstanceGenerator has no label and renders its own key; once the link is"
		+ "established the label table would name it, names being attested by a source or a save"
		REF @DECISION.WorldObjectNamesAreAttestedBySourceOrSave
		REF @DATATABLE.WorldObjectLabels
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-14 in the review of pull request 76, recorded on 2026-09-18"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST76

HYPOTHESIS ALinkedInventoryPlanetIsCarriedOnlyByAnExchangePlatform
	DESC "liPlanet, the planet of the inventory a world object is linked to, is carried only by an"
		+ "interplanetary exchange platform, and always names a planet other than the one the"
		+ "object stands on"
	UNTIL "a save carrying liPlanet on a world object that is not an"
		+ "InterplanetaryExchangePlatform1, or naming the planet the object stands on"
	OBSERVED_IN "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/section3-world-objects.schema.json::liPlanet"
	RATIONALE "The field appears 21 times over the 190338 world object entries surveyed, every time"
		+ "on an InterplanetaryExchangePlatform1 and every time naming another planet; 21"
		+ "occurrences of one object type prove a habit, not a rule of the game"
	SOURCE "Extracted from docs/save-format.md, what the reference saves say about the rarest"
		+ "three, on 2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
